        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Under nitrogen (drybox/Schlenk), Dy (0.75 g, 4.6 mmol), PhSeSePh (0.62 g, 2.0 mmol), iodine (1.27 g, 5.0 mmol), and Hg (0.05 g, 0.25 mmol) were combined in THF (60 mL) and stirred until the metal was consumed to give a yellow solution. Elemental Se (0.16 g, 2.0 mmol) was added, the mixture was stirred for 3 h, and then elemental S (0.032 g, 1.0 mmol) was added. After a day the orange solution was concentrated to ca. 40 mL, filtered, and layered with hexanes (12 mL). Yellow needle-shaped crystals formed in 12 days (0.36 g, 36%); they do not melt but turn dark brown at 253 °C.",
